			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Revise README with comprehensive architecture, project structure, and security documentation\n\nRewrite the Mountain README to provide a thorough technical overview of the Rust/Tauri native backend. Key improvements:\n\n- Replace 🏔️ emoji with ⛰️ for consistent branding across Land ecosystem documentation\n- Add comprehensive Overview section explaining Mountain's role as Common trait implementor, with performance metrics contrasting Electron\n- Annotate every component mention with its corresponding emoji (Cocoon 🦋, Vine 🌿, Wind 🌬️, Air 🪁) for visual scannability\n- Restructure Key Features as a dense paragraph-per-feature list, adding Extension Management, Over-the-Air Updates, Declarative Effect System details\n- Convert Core Architecture Principles from a list to a table with Key Components column\n- Add new System Architecture section with a connection path table documenting all IPC protocols (tauri::invoke, gRPC :50052, sky:// events, AirClient gRPC)\n- Include full Project Structure tree showing 30+ source directories and their roles (Air/, Cache/, Telemetry/, Track/, Update/, Vine/, etc.)\n- Expand In the Land Project section with table-formatted dependencies (Mist, Cache, Vine, Air) and connected components (Wind/Sky, Cocoon, Grove)\n- Add complete Getting Started section with prerequisites, build commands, feature flags (Development, MistNative), and run instructions\n- Add comprehensive Security section with 8-layer protection table (process isolation, gRPC boundary, permission system, message encryption, secure storage, certificate management, path security, message compression)\n- Update Related Documentation with new repos (Grove, Mist)\n- Revise Funding section with 🙏🏻 emoji\n- Document additional dependencies in tables (opentelemetry, posthog-rs)\n\nEstablishes README as the definitive entry point for contributors and integrators.",
			"SHA": "b72ae29e557f2b7156f02853ff5d46d9188d2c84"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
